AB  - The land surface is not Lambertian and instead exhibits strong anisotropic characteristics. Therefore, the Bidirectional Reflectance Distribution Function (BRDF) correction is crucial to ensure accurate, consistent, and comparable reflectance measurements. A directional correction leads to improved classification, time-series analysis, and multi-sensor data integration. In this chapter, we describe the characterization of BRDF. BRDF models, including empirical, physical, semi-empirical, and machine learning methods, are introduced. We present several BRDF correction applications based on BRDF models.
