AB  - Accurate and efficient identification of open-pit mining areas from remote sensing imagery is critical for global resource management and environmental monitoring. However, existing datasets are either low-resolution, region-limited, or incompatible with deep-learning pipelines, while current detection models struggle with complex backgrounds, multiscale targets, and real-time inference. To address these gaps, we present MAM-YOLOv10n, a lightweight yet powerful detector that integrates Convolutional Block Attention Module and C3 Transformer modules into YOLOv10n. This design boosts global context modeling and suppresses background clutter, yielding +1.71% mAP50 and +1.12% mAP75 over the baseline with negligible runtime cost. Concurrently, we release the North American Open-Pit Mine Target Detection dataset—the high-resolution (0.1–3 m), continent-scale benchmark covering 667 manually annotated mines across diverse mineral types, provided in both COCO and YOLO formats for immediate training use. Extensive experiments against YOLOv10n, Real-Time Detection Transformer, Faster R-CNN, EfficientNet, and Scale-Aware Feature Aggregation Framework demonstrate that MAM-YOLOv10n achieves the best accuracy–efficiency trade-off.
