AB  - Advancements in geological studies have been expedited by integrating deep learning techniques with Hyperspectral Imaging (HSI). We present a novel approach for identifying iron oxide with different compositions, in the Kiriburu region of India. We effectively address the challenges of spectral similarity and mixed pixel compositions present in hyperspectral data by combining Deep Embedded Clustering (DEC) with spectral unmixing. The Non-Linear Spectral Unmixing method processes pixel spectra to estimate endmember abundances, providing a fine-scale quantification of mineral composition. DEC clusters these separated spectral endmembers, successfully discriminating between iron oxide types. This integrative approach lowers the risk of misclassification, resulting in better spatial distribution and abundance mapping of the target mineral. The proposed approach presents a systematic data-driven approach towards reliable mineral exploration by leveraging accurate classification of iron-bearing minerals from hyperspectral input data.
