AB  - Mineral exploration is briskly on a switch made from pennon field observe to AI driven, data-centric overtures that upgrade efficiency and accuracy. Traditional methods, while foundational, may take a major amount of time, costly, and scarce in predictive accuracy. This work blend Remote Sensing (RS), Geographical Information Systems (GIS), and Artificial Intelligence (AI) to amplify mineral classification applying multi-spectral Landsat imagery and derived spectral indices that catch key mineralogical signatures. Automated raster data extraction is acted using QGIS and Python libraries, induce a region-specific dataset with 374 pixels and 13 predictor variables. Supervised machine learning classifiers, scilicet Multilayer Perceptron (MLP), Random Forest (RF), XGBoost (XGB), and Support Vector Machine (SVM), are proficient and amended, with MLP acquire the noble entire accuracy of 84.2%, proving superior ability to take nonlinear spectral patterns. The work depict that consolidate domain knowledge, satellite remote sensing, and AI can sanction efficient and elastic mineral classification, carry enhance exploration while shrink costs and environmental fixtures.
