AB  - Unsupervised segmentation of high-resolution multispectral satellite images is challenging due to spatial complexity and lack of labeled data. This study proposes a deep learning pipeline combining superpixel-based preprocessing, Vector Quantized Variational Autoencoder (VQ-VAE), and self-supervised contrastive learning. Using the POTSDAM dataset, the model extracts latent features from 32 × 32 patches and is trained with a mix of VQ-VAE, SimCLR, superpixel, and MS-SSIM losses. Gaussian Mixture Model (GMM) clustering generates pseudo segmentation masks, which are evaluated using cross-histogram analysis against ground truth. The method demonstrates robust segmentation performance without requiring manual labels, offering a scalable solution for remote sensing analysis.
