AB  - High Land Use classification accuracy is crucial for sustainable urban planning and environmental management, especially in rapidly urbanizing cities like Bangalore. This study uses high-resolution satellite imagery to test and compare the performances of three approaches: Traditional, Machine learning and Deep Learning methods. The overall classification performance of this parametric method was 88.1%, with a kappa statistic of 0.81. RF achieved good performance (90.9%) when employed here; its complex ensemble decision trees are effective for high-dimensional data and can create nonlinear relationships. Comparatively, the Deep learning model U-Net offered the best pixel-wise boundary retention and spatial feature extraction performance. It shows the effectiveness of a deep learning models for investigating the complexity of urban spectra and space.
